KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ function template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ lvalue parameters: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ member function template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Found while probing the comment in cpp_typecheck_type.cpp that the
placeholders of a pack_n >= 2 trailing-return fold are prvalues (sum_ref);
the other two cases regressed with d568a30139 (git bisect between 81c536b185
and 4810cde624), which made instantiate_template expand the unsubstituted
trailing return type together with the body; why the fold fails after that
is not analysed yet.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
